{"slug":"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/phrasal-verbs-idioms/","source":"students/subjects/english/core-grammar/phrasal-verbs-idioms.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Phrasal Verbs & Idioms — Core Grammar","description":"","subject":"english","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-4\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800\">← Back to Core Grammar</a></nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold mb-2 text-gray-800\">Phrasal Verbs &amp; Idioms</h1>\n      <p class=\"text-gray-600 mb-6\">Master the figurative expressions that make English natural and expressive. These are frequently tested in WAEC English Language examinations and are essential for fluent communication.</p>\n      \n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-500 p-4 mb-6 rounded-r\">\n        <h2 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\">📚 Learning Objectives</h2>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-700 space-y-1\">\n          <li>Understand what phrasal verbs and idioms are</li>\n          <li>Learn common phrasal verbs with their meanings</li>\n          <li>Master frequently used idioms and their origins</li>\n          <li>Apply these expressions correctly in sentences</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n\n    <!-- Section 1: Phrasal Verbs -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2\">\n        <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-800 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-sm\">1</span>\n        Phrasal Verbs\n      </h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"mb-4\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">What is a Phrasal Verb?</h3>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\">A phrasal verb is a combination of a <strong>verb + particle</strong> (preposition or adverb) that creates a meaning different from the original verb. The meaning is often <em>idiomatic</em>—you cannot guess it from the individual words.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"bg-indigo-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n        <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-800 mb-3\">Example: \"look up\"</h4>\n        <div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Literal meaning:</strong> look in an upward direction</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">\"She looked up at the sky.\"</p>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Phrasal meaning:</strong> search for information</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">\"I will look up the word in the dictionary.\"</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"mb-4\">\n        <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3\">Types of Phrasal Verbs</h4>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n          <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n            <h5 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800\">Separable Phrasal Verbs</h5>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">The object can come between the verb and particle</p>\n            <p class=\"text-green-700 text-sm\"><strong>Turn off the light.</strong> OR <strong>Turn the light off.</strong></p>\n            <p class=\"text-green-700 text-sm\"><strong>Take off your shoes.</strong> OR <strong>Take your shoes off.</strong></p>\n            <p class=\"text-amber-700 text-sm mt-2\">Note: With pronouns, separation is required: \"Turn <u>it</u> off.\" (NOT \"Turn off it.\")</p>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n            <h5 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800\">Inseparable Phrasal Verbs</h5>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">The object must come after the particle</p>\n            <p class=\"text-green-700 text-sm\"><strong>Look after the children.</strong> (NOT \"Look the children after.\")</p>\n            <p class=\"text-green-700 text-sm\"><strong>Run into an old friend.</strong> (NOT \"Run an old friend into.\")</p>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n            <h5 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800\">Intransitive Phrasal Verbs</h5>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">No object follows</p>\n            <p class=\"text-green-700 text-sm\"><strong>The car broke down.</strong></p>\n            <p class=\"text-green-700 text-sm\"><strong>Please sit down.</strong></p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Common Phrasal Verbs Table -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">📖 Common Phrasal Verbs (WAEC Essential)</h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n        <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse mb-4\">\n          <thead class=\"bg-indigo-100\">\n            <tr>\n              <th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Phrasal Verb</th>\n              <th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Meaning</th>\n              <th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Example</th>\n            </tr>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody class=\"divide-y\">\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">give up</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">stop trying; quit</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">Never <strong>give up</strong> on your dreams.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-indigo-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">break down</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">stop working; lose control emotionally</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">My car <strong>broke down</strong> on the highway.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">call off</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">cancel</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">They <strong>called off</strong> the meeting.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-indigo-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">carry on</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">continue</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">Please <strong>carry on</strong> with your work.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">come across</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">find by chance</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I <strong>came across</strong> an old photograph.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-indigo-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">fill in</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">complete (a form)</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">Please <strong>fill in</strong> this application form.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">get along</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">have good relations</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">They <strong>get along</strong> very well.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-indigo-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">give in</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">surrender; yield</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">He refused to <strong>give in</strong> to pressure.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">hold on</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">wait</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\"><strong>Hold on</strong>, I'll be with you in a minute.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-indigo-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">look after</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">take care of</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">She <strong>looks after</strong> her elderly mother.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">make up</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">invent; reconcile</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">She <strong>made up</strong> an excuse for being late.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-indigo-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">put off</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">postpone</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">They <strong>put off</strong> the meeting until next week.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">run out of</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">have none left</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">We've <strong>run out of</strong> sugar.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-indigo-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">take after</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">resemble (a parent)</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">She <strong>takes after</strong> her mother.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">turn down</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">reject</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">She <strong>turned down</strong> the job offer.</td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Section 2: Idioms -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2\">\n        <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-800 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-sm\">2</span>\n        Idioms\n      </h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"mb-4\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">What is an Idiom?</h3>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\">An idiom is a phrase or expression whose meaning cannot be understood from the literal meaning of its individual words. Idioms are culturally specific and must be learned as whole units.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n        <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-3\">Example: \"It's raining cats and dogs\"</h4>\n        <div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Literal meaning:</strong> Animals falling from the sky (impossible!)</p>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Idiomatic meaning:</strong> Raining very heavily</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 rounded-r mb-4\">\n        <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-2\">💡 Why Learn Idioms?</h4>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>They make your English sound more natural and native-like</li>\n          <li>They are frequently tested in WAEC exams</li>\n          <li>They help you understand native speakers and literature</li>\n          <li>They add color and interest to your writing</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Common Idioms Table -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">📖 Common Idioms (WAEC Essential)</h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n        <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse mb-4\">\n          <thead class=\"bg-purple-100\">\n            <tr>\n              <th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Idiom</th>\n              <th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Meaning</th>\n              <th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Example</th>\n            </tr>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody class=\"divide-y\">\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">a piece of cake</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">very easy</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">The exam was <strong>a piece of cake</strong>.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-purple-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">break the ice</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">start a conversation in a social setting</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">He told a joke to <strong>break the ice</strong>.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">burn the midnight oil</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">work or study late into the night</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">She had to <strong>burn the midnight oil</strong> to finish her project.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-purple-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">cost an arm and a leg</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">very expensive</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">That car <strong>cost an arm and a leg</strong>.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">crocodile tears</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">insincere tears; fake sadness</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">Don't be fooled by her <strong>crocodile tears</strong>.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-purple-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">eat one's words</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">admit one was wrong</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">He had to <strong>eat his words</strong> when he lost the bet.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">fish out of water</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">uncomfortable in a new environment</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I felt like a <strong>fish out of water</strong> at the party.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-purple-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">hit the nail on the head</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">be exactly right</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">You <strong>hit the nail on the head</strong> with your analysis.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">kill two birds with one stone</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">achieve two things at once</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">By cycling to work, I <strong>kill two birds with one stone</strong>—I exercise and save money.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-purple-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">let the cat out of the bag</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">reveal a secret</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">Don't <strong>let the cat out of the bag</strong> about the surprise party.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">once in a blue moon</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">very rarely</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">We only see our relatives <strong>once in a blue moon</strong>.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-purple-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">see eye to eye</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">agree completely</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">We don't always <strong>see eye to eye</strong> on politics.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">spill the beans</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">reveal secret information</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">Who <strong>spilled the beans</strong> about the surprise?</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-purple-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">under the weather</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">feeling sick or unwell</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I'm feeling a bit <strong>under the weather</strong> today.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-white\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-medium\">when pigs fly</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">something that will never happen</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">He'll apologize <strong>when pigs fly</strong>.</td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- WAEC Worked Examples -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">📝 WAEC-Style Worked Examples</h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n        <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\">Example 1: Phrasal Verb Meaning</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Question:</strong> Choose the meaning of the underlined phrasal verb:</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">\"The meeting was <strong>called off</strong> due to bad weather.\"</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700\">A. started B. postponed C. cancelled D. delayed</p>\n          <div class=\"mt-3 text-green-700\">\n            <strong>Solution:</strong> C. <strong>cancelled</strong><br>\n            <span class=\"text-sm\">\"Call off\" means to cancel something that has been planned.</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\">Example 2: Idiom Meaning</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Question:</strong> Choose the meaning of the underlined idiom:</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">\"The new smartphone <strong>cost an arm and a leg</strong>.\"</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700\">A. was damaged B. was very expensive C. was stolen D. was cheap</p>\n          <div class=\"mt-3 text-green-700\">\n            <strong>Solution:</strong> B. <strong>was very expensive</strong><br>\n            <span class=\"text-sm\">\"Cost an arm and a leg\" is an idiom meaning something is very expensive.</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\">Example 3: Using Phrasal Verbs</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Question:</strong> Replace the underlined word with a suitable phrasal verb:</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">\"She <strong>resembles</strong> her grandmother.\"</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700\">A. looks after B. takes after C. comes after D. goes after</p>\n          <div class=\"mt-3 text-green-700\">\n            <strong>Solution:</strong> B. <strong>takes after</strong><br>\n            <span class=\"text-sm\">\"Take after\" means to resemble a family member in appearance or character.</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-2\">Example 4: Contextual Meaning</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Question:</strong> Choose the meaning of the underlined expression:</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">\"The students <strong>broke the ice</strong> by introducing themselves.\"</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700\">A. broke something B. started a conversation C. caused trouble D. felt cold</p>\n          <div class=\"mt-3 text-green-700\">\n            <strong>Solution:</strong> B. <strong>started a conversation</strong><br>\n            <span class=\"text-sm\">\"Break the ice\" means to do or say something to relieve tension and start a conversation.</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Interactive Quiz -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">🎯 Quick Quiz</h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"space-y-4\" id=\"quiz-container\" data-bidemy=\"quiz\">\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. What does \"turn down\" mean?</p>\n          <div class=\"space-y-2\">\n            <label class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q1\" value=\"a\"> Accept</label>\n            <label class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q1\" value=\"b\"> Reject</label>\n            <label class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q1\" value=\"c\"> Turn around</label>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. \"Once in a blue moon\" means:</p>\n          <div class=\"space-y-2\">\n            <label class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q2\" value=\"a\"> Very rarely</label>\n            <label class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q2\" value=\"b\"> At night</label>\n            <label class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q2\" value=\"c\"> Very often</label>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Complete: \"Please ______ the TV. It's too loud.\"</p>\n          <div class=\"space-y-2\">\n            <label class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q3\" value=\"a\"> turn off</label>\n            <label class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q3\" value=\"b\"> turn down</label>\n            <label class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q3\" value=\"c\"> turn up</label>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        \n        <button class=\"bg-indigo-600 text-white px-6 py-2 rounded hover:bg-indigo-700\">Check Answers</button>\n        <div id=\"quiz-result\" class=\"mt-2 hidden bg-green-50 p-3 rounded text-green-700\"></div>\n      </div>\n      \n      \n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Practice Exercises -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">✍️ Practice Exercises</h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"space-y-6\">\n        <div>\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Exercise A: Match Phrasal Verbs</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">Match the phrasal verbs with their meanings:</p>\n          <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n            <li>run out of — <strong>?</strong></li>\n            <li>look forward to — <strong>?</strong></li>\n            <li>bring up — <strong>?</strong></li>\n            <li>set off — <strong>?</strong></li>\n          </ol>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-sm mt-2\">Options: a) start a journey b) have none left c) anticipate with pleasure d) raise (a topic/child)</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div>\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Exercise B: Complete with Idioms</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">Complete with appropriate idioms:</p>\n          <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n            <li>The math test was ______ (very easy).</li>\n            <li>She ______ when she realized her mistake. (admitted she was wrong)</li>\n            <li>We visit our grandparents ______ (very rarely).</li>\n            <li>The designer bag ______ (was very expensive).</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n\n        <div>\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Exercise C: Sentence Completion</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">Fill in with appropriate phrasal verbs:</p>\n          <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n            <li>The old car ______ (stopped working) on my way to school.</li>\n            <li>Please ______ (complete) this form carefully.</li>\n            <li>We have ______ (used all) our cooking gas.</li>\n            <li>Don't ______ (stop trying) just because it's difficult.</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <details class=\"mt-4 bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg cursor-pointer\">\n        <summary class=\"font-semibold text-green-800\">📋 View All Answers</summary>\n        <div class=\"mt-3 space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n          <p><strong>Exercise A:</strong> 1-b, 2-c, 3-d, 4-a</p>\n          <p><strong>Exercise B:</strong> 1. a piece of cake 2. ate her words 3. once in a blue moon 4. cost an arm and a leg</p>\n          <p><strong>Exercise C:</strong> 1. broke down 2. fill in 3. run out of 4. give up</p>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Video Resource -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">📺 Video Lesson</h2>\n      <div class=\"aspect-video bg-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n        <iframe class=\"w-full h-full\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/sXDlpRNkbcU\" title=\"Phrasal Verbs and Idioms Lesson\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen=\"\">\n        </iframe>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2\">Video: Common Phrasal Verbs in English</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">🔑 Key Takeaways</h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n        <div class=\"bg-indigo-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-800 mb-2\">🔄 Phrasal Verbs</h4>\n          <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n            <li>• Verb + particle combinations</li>\n            <li>• Meanings often not literal</li>\n            <li>• Some can be separated, some cannot</li>\n            <li>• Must be memorized as units</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\">💡 Idioms</h4>\n          <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n            <li>• Fixed expressions with figurative meaning</li>\n            <li>• Cannot translate literally</li>\n            <li>• Culturally specific</li>\n            <li>• Add color to language</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"mt-4 p-4 bg-yellow-50 rounded-lg\">\n        <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>💡 Exam Tip:</strong> In WAEC, the meaning of phrasal verbs and idioms is usually NOT literal. Always consider the figurative meaning based on context!</p>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-yellow-50 to-orange-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif}.card{ -webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(12px);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);} details[open] summary{border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb;padding-bottom:8px;margin-bottom:12px;}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}